From 5ff81ec6c02b249256675ff1633281d7c44d3f56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ide Stoutjesdijk <istoutjesdijk@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:12:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add fallback newsservers with a priority

Spotweb uses one newsserver per task. When it is down, or misses an
article because of a short retention or a block account, retrieving
or downloading fails.

Fallback newsservers can now be set under Settings, Newsservers, each
with a priority (0 is the highest) and the tasks it is used for:
retrieving spots and comments, NZB files and images, and posting.

- Reads by message-id use a try-list per article: on a 430 or a
  failure the next server is asked for the articles still missing.
- GROUP/XOVER/XHDR stick to the first server that accepts the GROUP,
  because article numbers differ between servers.
- Posting only moves on when connecting or logging in fails, so an
  article is never posted twice.
- A server that fails to connect is skipped for a few minutes; that
  state is shared between processes through a small file.

Without fallback servers the client pool hands out the plain transport,
so nothing changes for existing installations. See
docs/nntp-fallback-servers.md.
